CASE: matched common residual-frequency trajectory; 3 carrier centers [-75, 0, 75] Hz; occupied width 225 Hz
H_path: two shared complex path gains, delays [0, tau], each power 0.5; H_ind: independent flat complex gain per carrier, variance 1
Both hypotheses have equal per-carrier average signal power and the same circular complex AWGN variance; the common trajectory is conditioned out identically.
Bayes model priors are equal (1/2 each); KL is expected model-evidence separation, Bayes error is a finite one-triplet discrimination simulation, not bit decoding.
